      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.22,
      "end_seconds": 272.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "okay, you know, so I've had anxiety, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.14,
      "end_seconds": 288.74,
      "duration_seconds": 14.6,
      "text": "from what you've told me and what I found I'd lean towards a functional bowel pattern, with no alarm features. Another possibility is irritable bowel syndrome. I'm gonna order a coeliac blood test for bloating"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.68,
      "end_seconds": 294.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Uh do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.84,
      "end_seconds": 326.19,
      "duration_seconds": 31.35,
      "text": "try smaller meals and keep a food and symptom diary for four weeks. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. Do get help quickly if you see blood in the stool or lose weight. I'd like to see you again in six weeks. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
